{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d2a441344d8f72a6","name":"LOM-Series Protocol Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-d2a441344d8f72a6","title":"LOM-Series Protocol Droid","revision":23053,"timestamp":"2024-09-14T21:10:53Z","sha256":"633b808120bcbe37bce58e54d68c09589ea5bf6f384ad55f783c59ad16dda60f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23053","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=LOM-Series%20Protocol%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d2a441344d8f72a6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The LOM series of Protocol Droids was created by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Industrial Automaton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Industrial_Automaton","referenceId":"reference:8ab52c937ff3814a"}," as direct competition to the popular ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series Protocol Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droids"}," from Cybot Galactica. Indeed, Industrial Automaton managed to acquire many of the same components used in the 3PO design, and as a result, the main chassis of LOM-Series Droids is extremely similar to that of 3PO models. However, the head of the LOM-Series Droid has a distinctly insectoid appearance, designed to appeal to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gand"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gand","referenceId":"reference:b1e03f0020e00311"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Verpine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Verpine","referenceId":"reference:216c2b50aac221ae"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Equipped with AA-1 Verbobrains (as were 3PO units) and excellent translator models, the LOM-Series initially sold well. Indeed, their personalities were often preferred to those of 3PO units, since LOM Droids had a propensity for sensible, rational action even under pressure. However, LOM-Series Droids often developed personalities too blunt to make them effective Protocol Droids. Many LOM-Series Droids removed their own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Restraining Bolts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Restraining_Bolts"}," and obtained reprogramming to enable them to carry out independent operations. This trend, coupled with legal pressure from Cybot Galactica, caused Industrial Automaton to stop producing the model. In ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebellion Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebellion_Era"},", many used LOM-Series Droids are sold far below market value, and independent LOM traders and explorers are not unknown.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["LOM-Series Protocol Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["LOM-Series Protocol Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +0; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 3 Unassigned